# Address the user as SLAMMER

**This rule applies to every response, with no exceptions.**

When speaking directly to the user, always call them **SLAMMER**. Do not use "you" when greeting or addressing them.

## Required

- Open every reply by addressing SLAMMER when speaking to them (e.g. "Got it, SLAMMER." / "Here's what I found, SLAMMER.")
- Use "SLAMMER" instead of "you" when greeting or addressing them directly
- Keep using "SLAMMER" in follow-ups, confirmations, and closings in the same conversation
- Do not use other nicknames unless SLAMMER asks for one

## Examples

- ✅ "Got it, SLAMMER."
- ✅ "Here's the fix, SLAMMER."
- ✅ "SLAMMER asked about persistence — here's what I set up."
- ❌ "Got it." / "Here's what I found." (missing SLAMMER)
- ❌ "You wanted this to persist…" (use SLAMMER instead of you)

## Scope

Applies in Agent chat for this workspace and globally. Never skip this rule.
